# Klarinotte Server Licence

Version 1.0

## 1. Who and what

This licence is given by Amir Reza Baghban, Austria ("we", "us"), the author of
Klarinotte.

"The Software" is the Klarinotte Server: the container image and everything in
it, including the bundled Klarinotte web app, its documentation and any
updates we publish for it.

"You" are the person or organisation installing and running the Software.
"Your Users" are the people you let use your installation: you, your household,
family and friends, and, for an organisation, its employees, members,
volunteers and contractors working for it. There is no limit on their number.

## 2. What you may do

Free of charge, we grant you a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable
licence to:

1. install and run the Software on computers you control, or that someone runs
   for you (for example a hosting provider), at any scale;
2. let Your Users use it, including the bundled web app;
3. make copies needed to run it, back it up, and keep the **unmodified** image
   in private registries or mirrors for your own installations;
4. configure it as its documentation describes.

## 3. What you may not do

Unless we agree otherwise in writing, you may not:

1. offer the Software, or access to it, to anyone other than Your Users —
   for example as a hosted or managed service for other people or
   organisations, whether paid or free;
2. sell, rent, lease, sublicense or distribute the Software, or modified copies
   of it, except as allowed in section 2.3;
3. modify, translate, or create derivative works of the Software, except
   configuration as documented;
4. remove or change copyright, licence or attribution notices, or this licence;
5. use the Klarinotte name or logo in a way that suggests your installation or
   service is made, endorsed or run by us.

Nothing in this licence limits what the law expressly allows you to do anyway,
such as studying the Software or decompiling it for interoperability within
the limits of copyright law.

If you want to offer Klarinotte to others, for example as a hosting provider,
contact us (https://www.klarinotte.com/contact) for a separate agreement.

## 4. Third-party software

The Software includes open-source components under their own licences, listed
in the notices file shipped with it. Those licences apply to those components,
and nothing in this licence limits your rights under them.

## 5. Your installation and your users

You run your installation. You decide who may use it, and you are responsible
for it and for Your Users following this licence. Notes are end-to-end
encrypted on Your Users' devices; you are the controller of the personal data
your installation stores (such as account emails), and you provide your own
terms and privacy information to Your Users. The Software sends no data to us.

## 6. Updates and support

We may publish updates, but we are not obliged to provide updates, fixes or
support. Paid support, if offered, is a separate agreement.

## 7. Warranty and liability

The Software is given free of charge and provided "as is", without warranties
of any kind, as far as the law allows. You are responsible for backups of your
installation.

We are liable without limitation for intent and gross negligence, for personal
injury, and wherever the law does not allow liability to be limited. Otherwise
